<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle steady at $109.50/dressed - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle steady at $109.50/dressed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slaughter steers and heifers on a live and dressed basis steady, USDA said. Buyer inquiry good. Seller interest modest.</p>
<p>Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered</p>
<p>and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered ( paid on</p>
<p>hot carcass weights).</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers - Select and Choice 2-3 1200-1300 lbs -</p>
<p>67.00-68.00; dressed basis 109.00.</p>
<p>Slaughter heifers - Select and Choice 2-31050-1200 lbs -</p>
<p>67.50-68.00; dressed basis 109.00-109.50.</p>
<p>Confirmed - 2,500   For the week - 27,500</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
